# Hand helper text and vertical spacing

Add explanatory copy above the selected hand and move both card sections farther down the Hand sheet.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] A short helper paragraph appears above the Selected cards section.
- [ ] The helper explains that these are the selected player's current cards and that they affect Analysis values.
- [ ] Selected cards and Add cards are positioned farther down the screen than their current layout.
- [ ] The player selector remains clearly associated with the helper and card sections.
- [ ] The layout remains usable with an empty hand, stacked cards, Dynamic Type, and compact-height devices.
- [ ] Add, tap-to-remove, Clear, per-player switching, autosave, and dependent Analysis refresh behavior remain unchanged.
- [ ] The helper text is accessible and read before the card-editing sections.
- [ ] UI regression coverage compiles.
- [ ] Focused layout and accessibility checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.
